#%PAM-1.0
# Standalone DMS Lock service in simultaneous mode: face auth and the password
# field race, and whichever succeeds first wins. The password field stays live
# for the whole scan, so submitting the right password unlocks and drops the
# face flow; a successful face match unlocks and discards the pending password.
# This works across distributions because DMS generates `dankshell` from the
# host's own PAM policy (for example system-auth or common-auth).
# Keep DMS fingerprint authentication in its separate PAM context.
# Requires Gaze with the prompt-answering service gate (gaze >= the version
# that races for `dankshell-gaze-grosshack` without a controlling terminal).
auth      sufficient pam_gaze_grosshack.so
auth      include    dankshell
account   include    dankshell
password  include    dankshell
session   include    dankshell
